title: Error responses
tags: Daemon
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: Every daemon error is {"error": "<message>"} with a status code; the common statuses and what they mean.

An error answers `{"error": "<message>"}` (sometimes with more fields: a schema
violation carries a `violations` array) and a status:

|!Status |!When |
|`400` |a malformed body or query, an invalid pagination cursor, a `tree_ref` whose parent does not exist, that would make a cycle or pass depth 1000, a schema violation, an invalid schema file |
|`401` |no session token, or the wrong one ([[Session tokens]]) |
|`404` |no such repository (not loaded), metarecord, field row or task |
|`409` |a conflict with the current state: a repository already initialised there, a name already loaded, a store locked by another daemon, a reconcile or duplicate scan already running, a revert blocked by later changes, an unload while work runs |
|`423` |the repository is locked by a coordinated navigation (spec-event-log "Rollback lock") |
|`503` |the repository is still loading: watch its `load` task |
|`500` |an internal error — the store, the disk — the message saying which |

The CLI prints a daemon error on stderr as `error: <message>`, exit code 1.
